# Both images build from the repository root, so this list is what keeps a
# multi-hundred-megabyte build context from being sent to the daemon — and, more
# importantly, what keeps a local .env out of an image.

.git
.github

# ---- secrets: never in an image, regardless of .gitignore ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
service-account*.json
credentials*.json

# ---- Python ----
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# ---- Node ----
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*

# ---- Large artefacts nothing in a running container reads ----
docs/screenshots
# Neither image copies the harness: the API does not read it, and the frontend
# renders a committed copy of the report (frontend/src/data/evaluation-report.json).
# Excluded from the context so a build never uploads it.
evals
